            ],
            "public_requirement": "A transistor-level peak detector must accept pkdinp and pkdinn and produce a strictly increasing differential detector response at detp and detn.",
            "electrical_reason": "The detector consists of two electrically symmetric, independent common-emitter rectifier banks: both detp collector devices are driven only from pkdinp and both detn collector devices only from pkdinn. Equal-amplitude opposite-phase differential inputs therefore produce equal rectified averages on detp and detn, which cancel in the required differential output. There is no cross-coupled rectification, differential comparison, or other mechanism to convert differential RF amplitude into a usable detp-minus-detn signal."
          }
        ]
      },
