              "Xaut_p"
            ],
            "nodes": [
              "detp",
              "detn",
              "oa",
              "ag_ref",
              "agc",
              "gc"
            ],
            "public_requirement": "The required TIA, two RF stages, output buffer, detector, AGC, and selector must form a complete receiver whose finalp and finaln outputs meet the nominal, overload, power, and PAM4 requirements.",
            "electrical_reason": "Although the forward TIA-to-buffer path is present and agc is routed through the automatic selector to gc, the detector outputs detp and detn are disconnected from the AGC amplifier. Consequently the required detector-to-AGC-to-gc feedback path does not exist; the automatic gain setting is instead determined by oa versus ag_ref."
          },
          {
            "elements": [
              "Ralias_p",
              "Ralias_n"
            ],
            "nodes": [
              "outp",
              "outn",
              "finalp",
              "finaln"
            ],
            "public_requirement": "The required TIA, two RF stages, output buffer, detector, AGC, and selector must form a complete receiver whose finalp and finaln outputs meet the nominal, overload, power, and PAM4 requirements.",
            "electrical_reason": "finalp and finaln are attached to the actual buffer collector outputs only through 1 Mohm series resistors. This leaves the declared final outputs effectively floating and unable to drive a meaningful RF/output load; they act only as unloaded high-impedance aliases rather than as a physically usable buffered receiver output connection."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "summary": "The input TIA branches, two gc-controlled RF stages, and active differential buffer are coherently implemented. The detector topology cannot generate a substantive differential envelope from a balanced differential RF signal, and its outputs are not connected to the AGC amplifier. The resulting detector-to-AGC feedback loop is absent, while final outputs are only weakly alias-connected to the buffer."
